1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:11,168
Every morning, a field agent at an Indian lender starts the day with a spreadsheet of three hundred overdue loans, and no idea which twenty really matter.

2
00:00:11,218 --> 00:00:19,329
Visits go unverified, promises get lost in notebooks, and payments are sometimes marked as paid before the money ever arrives.

3
00:00:19,379 --> 00:00:25,042
This is RecoverIQ, our solution for QUASAR five point oh, problem statement one, fintech.

4
00:00:25,092 --> 00:00:25,858
One case.

5
00:00:25,908 --> 00:00:26,674
One trail.

6
00:00:26,724 --> 00:00:27,490
Full visibility.

7
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:33,171
We sign in as the administrator, so we can see every screen.

8
00:00:33,221 --> 00:00:42,880
The dashboard shows the overdue book, the money collected, the collection rate, the cost to recover every hundred rupees, the digital self-cure rate, and promises kept.

9
00:00:42,930 --> 00:00:48,482
Every rupee counted here was confirmed by the payment gateway, never typed in by hand.

10
00:00:48,532 --> 00:00:55,950
Below, we see daily collections, the mix of field, tele-calling and digital cases, and how old the overdue book is.

11
00:00:56,810 --> 00:01:02,686
New overdue accounts arrive from the lender's core banking system as a CSV or Excel file.

12
00:01:02,736 --> 00:01:04,167
Let's upload a sample.

13
00:01:04,217 --> 00:01:09,352
Six accounts are created, and one bad row is rejected with a clear reason.

14
00:01:09,402 --> 00:01:12,314
Now we upload the exact same file again.

15
00:01:12,364 --> 00:01:13,426
Zero new cases.

16
00:01:13,476 --> 00:01:18,240
One loan account always means exactly one case, so nothing is ever duplicated.

17
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:21,963
The case queue ranks every account by priority.

18
00:01:22,013 --> 00:01:23,734
Let's open the top case.

19
00:01:23,784 --> 00:01:26,213
The risk score comes with its reasons.

20
00:01:26,263 --> 00:01:30,109
Every point is explained, like days past due, and missed instalments.

21
00:01:30,159 --> 00:01:38,608
Next to it, a machine learning model estimates the chance that this borrower pays on their own within thirty days, with its top drivers.

22
00:01:38,658 --> 00:01:45,691
On the right, a manager can send a nudge, create a payment link, reassign the agent, or override the channel.

23
00:01:45,741 --> 00:01:48,170
Every one of these actions is recorded.

24
00:01:49,110 --> 00:01:51,343
Routing is driven by versioned rules.

25
00:01:51,393 --> 00:01:55,527
Let's lower the field visit threshold from seventy to fifty five.

26
00:01:55,577 --> 00:01:58,951
When we publish, the whole book is re-scored instantly.

27
00:01:59,001 --> 00:02:06,560
Affected cases move to field visits and are assigned to agents, and every case remembers which rule version decided it.

28
00:02:07,510 --> 00:02:14,728
Allocation matches cases to agents by pincode, distance, each agent's recovery record in that bucket, and spare capacity.

29
00:02:14,778 --> 00:02:19,170
One click on rebalance evens out the workload across the team.

30
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:21,808
Now, the field agent's phone.

31
00:02:21,858 --> 00:02:26,535
Rahul sees today's worklist, ranked, with the reason each case is on top.

32
00:02:26,585 --> 00:02:30,898
Field areas often have no signal, so let's switch the network off.

33
00:02:30,948 --> 00:02:32,353
The app keeps working.

34
00:02:32,403 --> 00:02:37,807
Rahul checks in at the borrower's address, and the GPS position and time are captured.

35
00:02:37,857 --> 00:02:39,988
He adds a note in Marathi.

36
00:02:40,038 --> 00:02:45,079
The borrower lost his job, but will pay the instalment once his salary comes.

37
00:02:45,129 --> 00:02:47,624
Both actions wait safely on the phone.

38
00:02:47,674 --> 00:02:51,260
When the network comes back, they sync automatically, exactly once.

39
00:02:52,210 --> 00:02:56,548
Back at the branch, the check-in appears on the live field map.

40
00:02:56,598 --> 00:03:00,204
Visits within three hundred metres of the address are verified.

41
00:03:00,254 --> 00:03:06,420
Visits that are too far away, have poor GPS accuracy, or show impossible travel speed are flagged.

42
00:03:07,310 --> 00:03:08,907
Now the most important rule.

43
00:03:08,957 --> 00:03:12,858
A case is marked paid only when the payment gateway confirms it.

44
00:03:12,908 --> 00:03:16,810
To collect, the agent shows a UPI QR code to the borrower.

45
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:24,119
The borrower scans it and sees a secure page in their own language, with the agent's verified identity.

46
00:03:24,169 --> 00:03:28,047
They pay through the gateway checkout, which runs in test mode.

47
00:03:28,097 --> 00:03:35,190
The gateway sends a digitally signed webhook to RecoverIQ, and only then is the payment accepted, with an instant receipt.

48
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:43,674
On the manager's screen, the case is now paid and confirmed, and the receipt is attached to the same case record.

49
00:03:43,724 --> 00:03:46,209
What if the same webhook arrives twice?

50
00:03:46,259 --> 00:03:47,295
We replay it.

51
00:03:47,345 --> 00:03:49,105
The result is, duplicate ignored.

52
00:03:49,155 --> 00:03:50,916
Money is never posted twice.

53
00:03:50,966 --> 00:03:54,537
And a forged webhook with the wrong signature is rejected.

54
00:03:54,587 --> 00:04:00,330
If a webhook is ever lost, a reconciliation job asks the gateway and posts what's missing.

55
00:04:01,250 --> 00:04:06,442
Recovery agents may only contact borrowers between eight in the morning and seven in the evening.

56
00:04:06,492 --> 00:04:11,684
Let's move the demo clock to eight thirty at night, and try to send an SMS.

57
00:04:11,734 --> 00:04:15,288
It's blocked, and the attempt is still logged with the reason.

58
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:19,220
The compliance report proves that nothing was ever delivered outside the window.

59
00:04:20,130 --> 00:04:27,219
Every action goes into a tamper-evident audit trail, where each row carries the hash of the one before it.

60
00:04:27,269 --> 00:04:31,727
Now let's simulate an insider editing a payment directly in the database.

61
00:04:31,777 --> 00:04:35,484
Verification immediately points to the exact row that was changed.

62
00:04:35,534 --> 00:04:38,490
Restore it, and the chain is intact again.

63
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,309
Promises to pay are tracked automatically.

64
00:04:41,359 --> 00:04:43,594
Let's jump the clock three days ahead.

65
00:04:43,644 --> 00:04:46,207
Promises that weren't kept break on their own.

66
00:04:46,257 --> 00:04:52,410
The first break sends the case for a field visit, and the second escalates it to the branch manager.

67
00:04:53,330 --> 00:05:03,504
Notes in Hindi, Marathi and English become a sentiment map of India, so managers can see where hardship is building, state by state and city by city.

68
00:05:03,554 --> 00:05:09,942
The leaderboard ranks agents only on gateway-confirmed money and GPS-verified visits, with the proof behind every point.

69
00:05:09,992 --> 00:05:19,030
And the learning loop retrains the model on real outcomes, compares it in shadow mode, and goes live only after a manager approves it.

70
00:05:19,930 --> 00:05:26,462
RecoverIQ covers all eighteen essential requirements, backed by automated tests and a full browser test.

71
00:05:26,512 --> 00:05:34,800
It runs with a single command, works offline in the field, and keeps every rupee and every contact provable.

72
00:05:34,850 --> 00:05:35,677
One case.

73
00:05:35,727 --> 00:05:36,555
One trail.

74
00:05:36,605 --> 00:05:37,432
Full visibility.

75
00:05:37,482 --> 00:05:38,310
Thank you.
